            "text": "In a triethylene glycol (TEG) gas dehydrator, the **liquid TEG phase** absorbs the water from the gas.\n\nThe **dry contacting streams** are arranged in **countercurrent flow**:\n- **Wet gas** enters the contactor near the bottom and rises upward.\n- **Lean (dry) TEG** enters near the top and flows downward.\n- The two streams contact on trays or packing, allowing the TEG to absorb water from the gas.\n\nSo, the **liquid phase absorbs the water**, and the **gas and glycol flow countercurrently**."
          }
